{
  "text": " We both had done the math and Kelly added it all up. If she had to let me go, I added it up, knew that I had lost her. Because I was never going to get off that island. I was going to die there, totally alone. I mean I was going to get sick or I was going to get injured. The only choice I had, the only thing I could control, was when, and how, and where that was going to happen. So, I made a rope and I went out to the summit to hang myself. I had to test it, you know, of course. And the weight of the log snapped the limb of the tree. I couldn't even kill myself to it. I wanted to. I had power over nothing. That's when this feeling came over me like a warm blanket. I knew somehow that I had to stay alive somehow. I had to keep breathing, even though there was no reason to hope. And all my logic said that I would never see this place again. So that's what I did. I stayed alive. I kept breathing. And then one day that logic was proven all wrong because the tide came in, gave me a sail. And now here I am. And back, you're Memphis talking to you. I have ice in my blindness. And I've lost her all over again. I'm so sad that I don't have Kelly. But I'm so grateful that she was with me on that island. And I know what I have to do now. I'm going to keep breathing. I guess tomorrow the sun will rise. Who knows what the tide could bring.",
